Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.04,0:00:07.24,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thanks for coming on, Eric Burn Arson from Modal.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.29,0:00:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could you explain the business a little bit and maybe how you got here?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.28,0:00:15.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, so we we build these as we put it as we build AI infrastructure.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.23,0:00:21.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we offer a bunch of compute a compute platform and a storage platform that enables a lot of
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.52,0:00:29.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,customers like Deck of Gone and Suno and Runway and Cognition and many others to to essentially build AI applications.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.48,0:00:32.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So what that means in practice is a lot of inference, a lot of sandboxes,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.64,0:00:37.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,sometimes training and fine-tuning, sometimes batch jobs and and other things.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.40,0:00:44.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we have basically built a a software SDK that enables customers to move really fast and and build this.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.28,0:00:49.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,We manage all the capacity underneath, make it easy to deploy and and scale and and run these things in production.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.84,0:00:52.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,So you were on Latent Space like 2 years ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:52.34,0:00:53.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,A lot has happened since then.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.02,0:00:55.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like how big were you back then?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:55.71,0:00:59.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like whatever numbers you can share and comparatively, yeah, how big are you now?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.80,0:01:01.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I actually don't remember where we were,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:01.48,0:01:08.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it's like it's probably like at least like 50x in terms of like revenue and users and usage and stuff like that, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:08.08,0:01:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I use it actually for like a side project that I have where Yeah, yeah, it's like yeah, turn like 2D images into 3D models.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.56,0:01:14.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:15.00,0:01:18.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,So yeah, I'm just hosting like a couple models there. do you think?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.30,0:01:18.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Any feedback?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:18.92,0:01:20.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,I love it.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.16,0:01:20.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.70,0:01:21.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.24,0:01:24.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I mean, yeah, that's why I use it over like any competitors or anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:24.48,0:01:24.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Good.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.04,0:01:31.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So before you started Modal, you were at Spotify and also like better.com That's right, yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:31.84,0:01:33.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, what were you doing at Spotify?
Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.72,0:01:39.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,I actually did a lot of different things at Spotify, but my main contribution was I built a music recommendation system, the first version.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.17,0:01:48.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I joined after school in 2008 2009 maybe and spent 7 years at Spotify and and most of that time was building basically from scratch a music
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.00,0:01:52.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,recommendation system and built up a small team and we launched a bunch of
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.53,0:01:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,features like related artists and discover weekly and and a bunch of other stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.08,0:01:59.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,So a lot of a lot of matrix factorization, a lot of compute-intensive stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.94,0:02:05.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and arguably like a lot of what sort of layer became the genesis of Modal was you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:05.68,0:02:10.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,just just building AI applications and realizing like the infrastructure sucks.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.75,0:02:12.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, there's got to be a better way to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.74,0:02:19.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, a lot of sort of you know, the rationale for for Modal was like kind of building a tool I always wanted to have throughout my years at Spotify.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.92,0:02:20.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.53,0:02:27.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, Modal was more of an offshoot of the stuff you learned at Spotify, not much from better.com?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:27.08,0:02:28.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Better better.com was a little bit of a side tour.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.71,0:02:30.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was kind of a roller coaster.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.11,0:02:32.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Long story about the company.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.20,0:02:32.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Talk about it separately.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.01,0:02:41.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, I was the CTO for for 5 years of better and grew the tech team from I think, you know, two to three 400.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:41.24,0:02:46.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I learned a lot about management and building teams and hiring and also learned a lot about developer productivity.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:46.19,0:02:48.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,Thought a lot about tools and things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.38,0:02:50.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did a lot more like full stack stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.20,0:02:55.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, yeah, I kind of came back to my what close to my heart, which is infrastructure and AI and machine learning after that.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.00,0:02:57.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,What was better.com doing again?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.68,0:02:58.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mortgages.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:58.36,0:02:59.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.24,0:02:59.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.68,0:03:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,How did you get into that?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.48,0:03:02.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, we don't have to spend too much time on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.08,0:03:03.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Just Yeah, no, it's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.21,0:03:12.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like this guy Zach Frankel who I didn't know at that time ended up recruiting me to better as the CTO and the company was 10 people and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:12.28,0:03:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,for whatever reason, you know, the the founder of Vishal very interesting guy, very very smart, a little crazy in in mostly positive ways.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:21.04,0:03:23.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,We got very well along.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:23.34,0:03:29.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, we yeah, we we started building it in in 2015 and I spent 5 years growing that company and then you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:29.83,0:03:33.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,eventually turned out that doing mortgages is pretty hard and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:33.18,0:03:37.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,interest rates went up very quickly after the pandemic and and that that caused a lot of issues at the company.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:38.03,0:03:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, by then I had already left.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:39.60,0:03:42.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,That was like 2020 2021 when you left?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:42.24,0:03:43.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, something like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.22,0:03:43.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:43.44,0:03:49.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, okay, you left before you had the idea for Modal or you left and then you started out on your own?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.64,0:03:50.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, it's It's to say.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.74,0:03:57.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I had a lot of random ideas when I left Better and and and I I I actually wasn't sure if I wanted to start a company.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.36,0:04:02.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was kind of just, you know, during the pandemic I I sort of almost took like a sabbatical.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.50,0:04:03.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,I had two kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:03.62,0:04:05.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean I still have two kids,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.51,0:04:08.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,but I mean at that time they were they were I think two and four and so
Dialogue: 0,0:04:08.81,0:04:13.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,I decided to hang out and took some time off and was kind of working like part-time,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:13.86,0:04:18.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,like hacking on certain things and wasn't sure maybe should do some consulting and I started
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.55,0:04:23.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,building stuff and I just got like super pumped about this idea that that eventually became Modal.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.99,0:04:27.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,But actually both, you know, Modal was like the I think the first thing I built that I got,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:27.91,0:04:31.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, that So so there were like a few attempts before then that that went nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.96,0:04:34.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but Modal was like the first idea was like, "This is kind of cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.42,0:04:35.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I should do this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:35.24,0:04:37.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is like this could be a really cool platform."
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.64,0:04:41.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Were the other ideas like also in a similar vein, like developer tools?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.48,0:04:45.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,The first thing was like some sort of web scraping thing, which went nowhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.12,0:04:47.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But actually, you know, in hindsight maybe could have gone somewhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:47.72,0:04:49.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And was this before the ChatGPT launch?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.76,0:04:50.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.21,0:04:51.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, 2021.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.12,0:04:53.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Okay. was late 2022, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:53.60,0:04:57.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then I I started building So So maybe actually to rewind a little bit context,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.20,0:05:01.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,like when I worked at Spotify I released an open-source framework called Luigi, which is like workflow orchestration.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.88,0:05:05.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's sort of the same category as Airflow and and Prefect and Daxter.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:05.60,0:05:11.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Sort of dated category to some extent, like people don't talk about it as much, but it for a while it was like, you know, got a lot of attention.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.68,0:05:13.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh anyway, I I never turned it into a business.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:13.79,0:05:20.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but a couple years later when in 2021 when I was thinking about business ideas or or things to work on,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:20.26,0:05:25.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,I kind of came back to workflow orchestration and I started hacking on a bunch of ideas of you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.51,0:05:29.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,running code in the you know, like basically orchestrating code running in the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:29.12,0:05:30.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And what I realized was like, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.93,0:05:36.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,at the end of the day like core puzzle piece is not just like orchestrating the compute, it's like executing the compute.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.25,0:05:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I was like, "That's kind of a bigger problem actually to solve."
Dialogue: 0,0:05:39.33,0:05:43.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,So in a way I actually like, you know, left it on the shelf and then said like,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.35,0:05:49.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,"Actually I'm going to like go to this other thing over here and I'll go back I'll get back to the workflow scheduling in a little bit,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:49.21,0:05:51.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,but but like you know, I never got back to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.24,0:05:53.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Long story short and and and I ended up building Modal,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.60,0:05:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is like the the focus is more like let's just figure out a way to make it easier to run code in the computer in the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.52,0:06:06.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and the focus was initially like fairly general purpose and it actually in a way like it's always we've kind of gone full circle more recently.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.72,0:06:08.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but we we focused on so many different applications.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.80,0:06:13.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was kind of the idea was like let's just make it super easy to run code in the in in the cloud.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.41,0:06:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Could be GPU code, could be AI machine learning, it could also be like data stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.52,0:06:21.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um and uh focused a lot on, you know, how do we scale it up?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:21.07,0:06:23.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do we make the developer experience awesome?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.40,0:06:30.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Realized super early that like in order to do that we'd have to go very deep in the stack and built our file system, built our container runtime.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:30.32,0:06:34.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and and did a lot of, you know, solved a lot of hard engineering challenges.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.26,0:06:39.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you mentioned ChatGPT, that was actually not quite the killer app,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.06,0:06:44.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,but it like if you remember like that fall another thing came out around the same time, which was stable diffusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:44.82,0:06:48.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And stable diffusion turned out to be a killer app for our for what we're building at that time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.76,0:06:51.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We were only four or five people at that time.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.08,0:06:55.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,So uh we started seeing a lot of people coming to us and wanting to run uh stable diffusion model.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.65,0:07:01.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then we realized that that that made us realize like maybe gen AI inference is actually really good use case for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.24,0:07:02.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,And how were you finding it?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.32,0:07:04.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm just like compulsive tweeter.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:04.33,0:07:09.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was even more like now like I'm too distracted by building a company, but I always like tweeted a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.55,0:07:10.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was blogged a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:10.39,0:07:13.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I think I had a little bit of a following and so, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:13.59,0:07:20.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,in the early days uh like a lot of what drove the growth is just like me just compulsively just like tweeting about Modal and like what I was
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.84,0:07:24.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,building and getting people excited and writing long blog posts about where the cloud
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.17,0:07:27.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,is going and all these things and I call it a bit like founder-led marketing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:27.52,0:07:30.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I was like feel like you kind of have to lean into like what you're good at and
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.28,0:07:35.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,like what I'm good at is like I guess like just posting and being terminally online and and so,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:35.07,0:07:37.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, like work it it's it's still like, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.94,0:07:43.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think a lot of our growth is we're just kind of good at social media and just like being, you know, online a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.44,0:07:43.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Nice.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.84,0:07:46.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,How long until you had your first customer?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.96,0:07:50.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It took a while cuz we started Also, did you raise like early on?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:50.60,0:07:51.62,Sub,,0,0,0,,We didn't raise for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.67,0:07:53.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,I actually self-funded it for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:53.58,0:07:56.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Even with up until the first few employees.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.32,0:08:02.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Which in a way was like kind of nice cuz it made me really like frugal about money and like wanting to see like ROI.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.38,0:08:05.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,I wasn't taking out a salary for a while, for a long time actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.75,0:08:08.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,At some point it became a problem because I needed the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.97,0:08:14.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we didn't raise for a while and um until early 2022 raised a seed round.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.20,0:08:17.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so at that point I'd already been working on it for about a year.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.28,0:08:24.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Akshat joined us as CTO and co-founder in in about about 5 years ago, about now, August maybe 2021.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.88,0:08:30.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But then it took until like basically like late 2022 for us to see any meaningful revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.72,0:08:32.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I guess that's when ChatGPT came out.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.40,0:08:37.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and and Stable Diffusion then in in our case was the main thing that sort of So so we went from like,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:37.91,0:08:45.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, $100 a month in like I think like November 2022, and the next month we did like $2,000 a month.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:45.06,0:08:50.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then like January 2023 we did like $30,000 all of a sudden.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:50.68,0:08:55.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know, so so finally I felt this like massive just like anxiety thing off my chest.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.02,0:08:58.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm like, maybe this is actually like we're onto something.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:58.66,0:08:59.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels like we're onto something.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:59.69,0:09:04.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then 2023 we grew very fast and I guess we've been growing very fast since then basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.36,0:09:10.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,That 30K a month moment, was that just like a couple big customers or was it like very like diverse?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:10.72,0:09:16.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's just one and I don't I don't know if I ever talked about like who that was and if they even know it, but I think they suspect it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:16.81,0:09:18.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was a company in New York called Mage.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.60,0:09:21.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're doing like a Stable Diffusion company.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:21.05,0:09:29.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,So at some point, you know, in in in the first I think first quarter of of 2020 three, I think they were like 80-90% of our revenue.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.93,0:09:35.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but then after that, you know, it started diversifying a little bit and late 2023 we we got Suno as a big customer.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.92,0:09:38.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,They were a big chunk of our revenue for a while, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:38.05,0:09:42.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,But then, you know, it's over time like we actually have really good revenue diversification now.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.72,0:09:43.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:43.20,0:09:47.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,For the stable diffusion stuff, I remember using it for like comfy UI.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:47.87,0:09:51.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm assuming a lot of people you were using comfy UI, like running comfy UI workflows on it.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.92,0:09:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Some people were, but but I I think the people that were using Modal, they tended to be more like low-level stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:57.04,0:09:58.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like they did like complicated stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.36,0:10:00.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,What they like with Modal is like it's always been pretty hackable.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:00.64,0:10:01.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.36,0:10:01.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,So,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.57,0:10:08.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,they they deployed their own custom workflows with adapters and custom in friends and and a lot of optimizations and and all the all the
Dialogue: 0,0:10:08.89,0:10:15.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,stuff we had done in order to get the developer experience to be really good turned out to be really good for also running production workloads.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.72,0:10:18.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh cuz auto scaling turns out to be actually a very similar problem.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.72,0:10:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you want to scale up containers up and down very fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:21.72,0:10:26.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so, we we just happened to be like very well positioned to to capture a lot of those workloads in the early days.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.08,0:10:28.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did tools for auto scaling like not exist?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.58,0:10:30.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like why did you have to build those yourself?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.60,0:10:39.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,In general, like my thesis is like, you know, every new sort of era of like, you know, technology kind of runs up against limitations of of tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:39.59,0:10:46.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you know, whether that's you look back, you know, like the web or the cloud or, you know, mobile or PCs or or, you know, AI or whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.01,0:10:50.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so I I I think, you know, it's of often the case that tools exist.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:50.72,0:10:53.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but they're often not like particularly good.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.87,0:10:58.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and often you you kind of need to rethink a lot of those tools in order to reap the benefits of,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:58.21,0:11:02.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, and and really, you know, turbocharge and start building for this new world.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.06,0:11:06.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then you saw this with cloud, you know, we had to invent things like Kubernetes and Docker and things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.35,0:11:14.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then in in in a similar way, you know, like with with gen AI, you could build these things on the sort of prior generation of tools.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:14.05,0:11:18.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you you can't you can build these things on top of Kubernetes and Docker and and these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:18.36,0:11:21.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but but those technologies are built for a very different type of workload.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.22,0:11:24.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,They're built for a very sort of steady work steady back-end workloads.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.51,0:11:31.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,They have an even, you know, steady number of requests, like running at a pretty low utilization cuz CPUs are normally pretty cheap.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.54,0:11:31.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:31.93,0:11:35.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,people don't really worry so much about cost and but now you're entering this new world and
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.82,0:11:41.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,you have you know very expensive GPUs you want to manage capacity and and utilization you have very
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.49,0:11:46.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,large models that you need to load over network into CPU into GPU and and it it turns
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.86,0:11:50.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,out like a lot of these tools like you know like they're they're just not built for that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.85,0:11:56.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so we felt that you know we we had to rebuild a lot of that you know building our own I mentioned the file system but we also spent
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.04,0:11:59.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,a lot of time over the last few years like building you know some really
Dialogue: 0,0:11:59.96,0:12:04.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,cool stuff around like CPU snapshotting GPU snapshotting and auto we built our own auto
Dialogue: 0,0:12:04.75,0:12:08.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,scaler and scheduler and and and and all kinds of capacity management tools and we
Dialogue: 0,0:12:08.76,0:12:12.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,kind of feel like you have to do that because like you can't build you
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.39,0:12:19.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,know for this new generation of of software on top of you can't build like a wrapper on top of the old stuff in order to to do the new stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.13,0:12:21.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,You kind of need to start over a little bit from scratch.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.72,0:12:26.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So I guess like the auto scaling stuff like did you did you see any like um
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.84,0:12:32.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,weird behaviors on the platform like was there anything that like broke while you guys were scaling?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.44,0:12:35.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean capacity is always from time to time been been a challenge like how do you
Dialogue: 0,0:12:35.70,0:12:41.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,get like you know hundreds and thousands and tens of thousands of GPUs so that's that's always challenging.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:41.30,0:12:47.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had to go multi-region very early so I think that was like kind of a fateful decision in hindsight like doing that and kind of just biting
Dialogue: 0,0:12:47.79,0:12:53.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,the bullet and building it like we always thought of like our our capacity management is like one big pool like it's like one big pool of it
Dialogue: 0,0:12:53.76,0:12:59.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,over the the entire world like we don't think of it as like separate clusters running in each region and so that that was like one of the
Dialogue: 0,0:12:59.71,0:13:06.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,like very consequential decisions we made early to kind of think about it that way so I don't know if there's like been like you know specific issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.31,0:13:13.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean we've obviously had bugs and you know outages and I hate you know as much as I you know would love for Modal to be 100% uptime you know
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.98,0:13:17.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,and and I think recently we've basically hit four or five nines but throughout the history
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.63,0:13:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,of Modal of course we've had you know run up against scaling issues things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.28,0:13:25.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,The GPU market and well actually before that.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:25.15,0:13:30.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,So So, guys use AWS like GCP, like all these cloud providers underneath?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:30.70,0:13:33.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, do you also buy any infrastructure or no?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:33.64,0:13:36.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Let's talk a bit about like cloud capacity because I think it's actually changed a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:36.60,0:13:44.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, in in the first few years, we did we got almost all the capacity pretty much from from the hyperscalers, spot and on-demand capacity,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.23,0:13:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,mostly spot capacity, running in all the different regions, you know, using uh initially AWS, but also GCP and and over time Azure.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:52.72,0:14:01.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we we started renting some capacity from Oracle pretty early cuz we wanted um 8 tons and 8 100s, and we got really good rates on those.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.52,0:14:05.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and and over time we added a couple more clouds like doing reservations,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.24,0:14:13.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,but but like still up until like actually end of last year, like most of our capacity was either spot or or 1-year reservations.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.64,0:14:16.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Spot means you're just like renting it right there and then Exactly.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.71,0:14:19.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and it's also preemptible, which we had to deal with.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:19.16,0:14:25.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um but but it sort of works in aggregate cuz you can sort of just, you know, aggregate capacity from many, you know, hundreds of regions, basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.48,0:14:28.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, that that that model worked really well until we started running up again.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:28.84,0:14:33.01,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, first of all, like Modal started growing like very fast, and so we needed more capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:33.06,0:14:36.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,But fundamentally, also like the cloud market started changing a lot.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.38,0:14:44.30,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um so, in the last year, basically, now in order to get the capacity we need, we have to work with a much larger set of clouds.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.35,0:14:47.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,We actually work with almost 25 clouds at this point.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.68,0:14:52.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,And in many cases, um in order to get the capacity we want, like we we have to go and do,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:53.01,0:14:58.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, 3-plus year deals, and you have to pay a meaningful amount of money up front.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:58.11,0:15:00.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and and you're locking in pricing on on a 3-year term, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.92,0:15:08.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you know, like and and and so we have to spend the entire, you know, last 6 to 9 months, like, you know, kind of rethinking how we get capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:08.77,0:15:13.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had to build a whole procurement like desk, like we have like four guys working full-time, basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.40,0:15:19.08,Sub,,0,0,0,,All they're doing is like procuring capacity, calling the clouds, you know, doing deals, vetting the capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.13,0:15:24.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,We had to build a whole engineering team basically you have people just like managing like bare metal capacity from all
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.93,0:15:31.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,over the world and dealing with network issues and bad drives and GPUs falling off the bus and and all these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.95,0:15:33.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,We don't own capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.40,0:15:33.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mhm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:34.00,0:15:38.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,We rent all the capacity so far, um you know, on on on typically these 3-year deals.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:38.55,0:15:40.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that's like a big decision.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.16,0:15:40.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like should we buy?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.90,0:15:43.69,Sub,,0,0,0,,Should Should we you know, you know, or should we keep renting?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.74,0:15:46.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I'm actually like not like mega dogmatic about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:46.76,0:15:50.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think renting is nice because there's a certain amount of capital efficiency to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.64,0:15:56.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,If you're buying, you know, like I mean, first of all, there's an obvious like operational complexity of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:56.72,0:16:04.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like you have to, you know, deal with vendors and suppliers and and, you know, power and and and cables and and all kinds of stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.32,0:16:06.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's also, you know, financial complexity to it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:06.42,0:16:07.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like how do you fund it?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:07.40,0:16:12.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like should you raise equity, you know, and and you can raise a billion dollars and and go buy hardware for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:12.72,0:16:14.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's a very diluted way to do it.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:15.01,0:16:17.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um you can raise debt, but you know, if you raise debt, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.76,0:16:22.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,you you typically want to have like locked-in long-term revenue to to to pay the interest rates.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.86,0:16:25.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,So that's also not trivial.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:25.28,0:16:31.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, you know, like we look at the economics, we look at the the the operational complexity, we look at the risks.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:31.54,0:16:35.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh it's a complex trade-off and and we're open to to to to buying.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.20,0:16:37.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,We we're we're sort of There's all other constructs, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:38.01,0:16:44.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we're it's To get the capacity we need for for 2027, it's going to take a lot of work on on,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.10,0:16:47.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, going a lot of different avenues to to to lock it up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.44,0:16:51.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, do you have to hire a lot of like finance people to do all this stuff or not really?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.04,0:16:56.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, I've had to spend a lot of time on this and we we've had to to to spend a lot of time on this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.79,0:17:03.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I I do think over time, I mean, there there is a lot of, you know, these are very expensive assets, uh the hardware.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:03.16,0:17:05.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, I think I mean, it's kind of staggering.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.96,0:17:12.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,You're starting to see like AI investment starting to become like several percentage points of of of GDP of the US and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:12.69,0:17:17.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,starting to see like interest rates in in America shooting up in the last few weeks.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.36,0:17:18.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I I mean,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:18.09,0:17:25.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I like at this stage like you know and then you go and look at the neoclass like these are very very sophisticated financial engineering companies and
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.24,0:17:31.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,so yeah we we look at that and you know we look at all the options and and it's possible we might have to do similar things ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.80,0:17:40.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't want to like I would rather focus on being you know like a very lean software company like doing the things we're good at.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.49,0:17:46.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't think it's good in general for software companies to own hard assets you know in the same way as
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.89,0:17:53.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,like should you own your office like I I don't think that's necessarily the right uh solution for for most companies.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.62,0:17:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,But of course like in order to get the capacity we want like you know everything is on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:57.32,0:18:02.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah and I guess the supply is going to be constrained for a while so you kind of have to do that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.04,0:18:06.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like do you do you agree with that or do you think this is just like a moment in time?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:06.36,0:18:07.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't necessarily agree with that.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.65,0:18:14.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean like Nvidia's delivering you know several hundred thousand black walls you know a month right and and I I I don't want to say like
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.19,0:18:23.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,the market is like 100% efficient but like you know in general like if you're willing to pay a high price uh you can get GPU capacity right?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:23.20,0:18:29.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like if you're willing to pay more than everyone else and and of course Anthropic and Open AI is buying up as much as they can
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.22,0:18:33.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,and but fundamentally like there's constantly supply coming on the market and and
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.23,0:18:37.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,so I don't I don't necessarily think it's like a fully cornered resource.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:37.76,0:18:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Prices are going up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.60,0:18:42.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and I do think it's worth kind of reflecting on that as like the normal
Dialogue: 0,0:18:42.76,0:18:47.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,state of hardware is like it's like out of gravity like eventually hardware prices always go down.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.24,0:18:52.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we're a little bit in like a weird sort of period of time where like hardware prices are going up.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:52.16,0:18:56.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,And you know it it it's hard to say you know how how long is this going to last you know could be
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.14,0:19:02.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,another 6 months could be another 36 months like it's really hard to to to know how how how long and but but I
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.25,0:19:07.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,I fundamentally don't know if like it's it's true to say like you know you need to buy capacity in order to to
Dialogue: 0,0:19:07.80,0:19:14.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,to me that's a little bit the sort of almost like the uh great toilet paper shortage of you know the pandemic or whatever,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.25,0:19:14.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,right?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:14.52,0:19:17.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, you know, at least this like, you know, run on the bank type situations.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:17.92,0:19:21.61,Sub,,0,0,0,,And but that being said, like, you know, capacity is going to be tight for a while.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:21.66,0:19:23.10,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and, you know, prices are going up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.15,0:19:28.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, luckily, I think you know, it's not even necessarily bad for us if prices go up cuz cuz,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:29.03,0:19:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, scarcity also means like we can charge more from our customers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:32.00,0:19:37.40,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and, you know, and the fact that we have a lot of reservations locked in at a rate means like to some extent,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.45,0:19:40.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,we effectively like long GPU prices already.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.80,0:19:45.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, so, um, I I don't necessarily worry too much about prices going up.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.60,0:19:47.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,I do worry more about actually prices collapsing.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.65,0:19:50.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I don't think that's going to happen anytime soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.22,0:19:53.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh, but I think that would be a quite bad thing for a lot of the players in the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:54.00,0:19:55.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Why would that be bad?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.16,0:20:00.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it would be bad for if for anyone who's locked in a lot of supply.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.56,0:20:02.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, cuz they paid way too much in They paid too much.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.59,0:20:05.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, the so there's a risk of buying at the top, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.08,0:20:07.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and again, like I I don't worry about that that much.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.58,0:20:11.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I don't I don't think it's going to be like, you know, it's going to happen anytime soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.42,0:20:15.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,But like, you know, like I said, like hardware prices in the very long run, they tend to go down.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:15.98,0:20:18.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, it's it's worth, you know, reflecting on that, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:18.71,0:20:23.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,Right right like right now, I think I think your your capacity is constrained.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.84,0:20:28.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that leads to sort of, you know, in economic terms, there's a scarcity rent, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:28.48,0:20:30.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, who captured the scarcity rent?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.80,0:20:32.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think it primarily goes to two places.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:32.68,0:20:36.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,Mostly Nvidia, but of course, but also to some extent, Neo Clouds.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:36.22,0:20:42.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, Neo Clouds and in general, like, you know, anyone owning capacity has better economics.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:42.42,0:20:47.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, that's undeniably true today with capacity being constrained.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:47.96,0:20:51.94,Sub,,0,0,0,,Long term, you know, in the very long run, I don't think that's necessarily entirely true, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:51.99,0:20:55.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, there's always going to be a little bit of a premium you can get from owning GPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:55.68,0:21:01.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,But is it worth the risk, you know, is it worth the risk like holding these like very expensive assets on your balance sheet?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:01.95,0:21:02.85,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm not so sure.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.90,0:21:04.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,But, you know, we're going to see.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:04.22,0:21:06.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, it's going to take a a years to get through this.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:06.08,0:21:09.88,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and and in the long run, you know, we might own some, we might rent some,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.93,0:21:14.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe a combination, maybe do some other crazy stuff, joint ventures, who knows.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:14.56,0:21:17.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe some complex SPVs or whatever.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:17.70,0:21:19.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um everything is on the table.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:19.32,0:21:22.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,How do you compete with OpenAI and Anthropic in buying GPU capacity?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:22.51,0:21:25.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm assuming they'd want to like buy up literally everything that's available.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.04,0:21:32.42,Sub,,0,0,0,,They are and and I and I think what you're seeing is um you know, a lot of the the the price is going up is a reflection of that.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:32.47,0:21:35.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,That being said, you know, Nvidia is shipping a lot of stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.03,0:21:40.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think also like to some extent like Nvidia's like kind of prefer a little bit of a diversification.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:41.04,0:21:44.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like they don't want like, you know, small amount of large buyers.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.19,0:21:49.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,In much in the same way as you see, you know, hyperscalers getting a little bit of a constrained allocation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:49.36,0:21:55.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh I I think, you know, also Nvidia prefers to see, you know, a lot of new clouds and a lot of alternative clouds like getting more allocation.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:56.01,0:22:03.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,And I think a little bit what we see in the market is also this is more speculation, but I but I think we see,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.38,0:22:10.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, smaller clouds that are a little bit more sort of risky to work with being more of an opportunity for us.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:10.70,0:22:13.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like where, you know, maybe Nvidia is all right,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:13.78,0:22:20.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,Anthropic and OpenAI my feeling is like they prefer to buy from like the the tried and
Dialogue: 0,0:22:20.17,0:22:23.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,true Uh and part of it is also because they had to do a lot of training runs,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.10,0:22:24.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,so they need to have like very large blocks.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:24.82,0:22:32.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,But there's plenty of capacity out there, you know, you can get 32 nodes in Armenia, you can get 128 nodes in Indonesia.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:32.37,0:22:37.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, you know, like we love that kind of Like, you know, so so we can go out there and like get a lot of,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:37.37,0:22:41.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, smaller capacity all over the world pretty good prices.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.16,0:22:46.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is it pretty much just like if someone offers you like a certain number of GPUs, like that's all you care about?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:46.09,0:22:52.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is there nothing like, oh, you care about like how reliable it is, you know, is it just some like janky warehouse that someone has these in?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:53.00,0:22:55.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, sometimes it's kind of a janky warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:55.22,0:22:58.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,It feels like, you know, but but like we do have like a spec sheet basically.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:59.00,0:23:01.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like when we talk to vendors, the first thing we do is we send them a spec sheet.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.91,0:23:04.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,We say, "We need this number of IOPS.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.08,0:23:08.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need, you know, like the CPU needs to be at least at least, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:08.64,0:23:11.96,Sub,,0,0,0,,have have this many, you know, whatever the pass mark scores or whatever it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:12.02,0:23:19.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,We need to see like, you know, minimum, you know, north north south bandwidth egress and and ingress."
Dialogue: 0,0:23:19.36,0:23:22.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh so so we do have a list of requirements.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:22.08,0:23:26.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,Often we try to do like an acceptance testing period where we get like one node and then run some tests.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.02,0:23:31.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Over time, you know, like to some extent it also involves a little bit of a leap of faith.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.32,0:23:35.72,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, sometimes we sign very big commitments, you know, tens or hundreds of millions of dollars,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:35.77,0:23:39.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,and we start working with the vendor that we still don't fully know.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.33,0:23:42.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, over time like you know, we'll see.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.19,0:23:46.77,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, and and and I think over like a little bit of like is there's a little bit of sort of just,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:46.82,0:23:52.29,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, our own sort of like, you know, how like semi-analysis has like a cluster max.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.34,0:23:56.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I kind of feel like we almost like have our own like modal max score internally.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.44,0:23:59.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I know which vendors I like more than others, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:59.44,0:24:05.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,like and and and we sort of prefer to do additional deals with the vendors that we've seen, you know, very good reliability.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:05.44,0:24:10.57,Sub,,0,0,0,,Not just that also, like it it's not just reliability, it's also are they very responsive when when we have,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.62,0:24:15.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, support issues, do they fix the issues we ask for, the turnaround time.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:15.09,0:24:18.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,If things go down, you know, how quickly do they fix it, like things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:18.44,0:24:23.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Do you agree that the demand for intelligence is basically infinite?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:23.52,0:24:28.21,Sub,,0,0,0,,And if so, like why wouldn't you just buy up as much as you as much capacity as possible?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:28.26,0:24:31.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then like if you overbuy, you can just like sell it to somebody else.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:31.20,0:24:36.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's very easy to say when there's like a scarce resource, like let's just buy as much as you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:36.96,0:24:41.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think, you know, first of all, like if we bought it today, we couldn't utilize all of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:41.17,0:24:43.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we could use utilize a lot of it, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:43.28,0:24:46.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,But like We can sell it off to somebody else who wants to use it, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:46.24,0:24:53.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think the challenge is like if there was like something in the market that happens, there are a lot of correlations that happen at the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:53.57,0:25:04.36,Sub,,0,0,0,,If, you know, price is going down and utilization going down and the market for reselling capacity goes vanishes at the kind of the same time.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.41,0:25:09.52,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm sitting here and like I'm I'm extremely aggressive like buying capacity every day and like raising money to buy,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.57,0:25:11.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, so overall I'm I'm very bullish,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:11.78,0:25:19.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,but like I do want to point out and like, you know, like there are tail risks here and and when those tail risks happen like it could be get very bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:19.52,0:25:20.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,Part of it is like maybe I'm, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:21.04,0:25:24.74,Sub,,0,0,0,,I'm just old and I've seen this in the past like I was actually had my first job in 1999
Dialogue: 0,0:25:24.79,0:25:30.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,so I saw the dot com crisis and I've seen the great financial crisis and things like that and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:30.20,0:25:35.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,like I want to build a company that that is around for like 20 to 30 50 more years, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.52,0:25:42.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like and and so, you know, I I think we can certainly go out and like buy an insane amount of capacity right now and try to just corner the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:42.48,0:25:44.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,But you know, do you know about the Hunt brothers?
Dialogue: 0,0:25:44.55,0:25:46.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's like a legendary story in trading.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:46.98,0:25:49.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,They try to corner the silver market.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:49.32,0:25:50.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,It fell spectacularly.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:50.65,0:25:57.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, you know, so it's a cornering the market I I think in general like it can be um not not so good idea.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:57.32,0:26:00.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um, and but but we are in general very very aggressive.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:00.51,0:26:02.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but we're we're ramping up, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.03,0:26:07.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,like at an at an aggressive plan that basically matches our demand growth and matches where we want to
Dialogue: 0,0:26:08.04,0:26:13.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,try to get to at the end of next year in terms of run runway or run rate I mean.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:13.24,0:26:17.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are you only buying up Nvidia stuff or also like, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.28,0:26:22.51,Sub,,0,0,0,,maybe a capacity from other types of companies like are you guys looking at Cerebrium and We're we're looking at it.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:22.56,0:26:26.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I I think the alternative accelerators are starting to get very interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:26.10,0:26:31.44,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's you know, ironically like every every year in the last five maybe even 10 years I've been saying, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:26:31.49,0:26:35.86,Sub,,0,0,0,,like next year it's going to be the year of like non Nvidia accelerators and and then I'm always wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:35.91,0:26:40.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,But but I do think 2027 might be the year of non Nvidia accelerators finally.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:40.28,0:26:46.28,Sub,,0,0,0,,So we'll we'll see if I'm wrong this year, too, but so I I you know, AMDs are starting to get like really good scores on certain things.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:46.33,0:26:51.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think, you know, TPUs are are obviously used very, you know, widely internally at Google.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.60,0:26:52.82,Sub,,0,0,0,,They seem to work really well.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:52.87,0:26:54.09,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I don't know much about Tranium.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.14,0:26:57.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I don't feel like I see quite as But, you know, the the team is very good.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:57.44,0:27:00.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,I know they're working on a lot of the software stuff.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.48,0:27:02.12,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, hardware is hard in a in a certain way.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:02.17,0:27:03.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, software is like easier.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.19,0:27:07.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,And that makes me feel like, you know, if we just fix the sort of software layer for these accelerators,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:07.08,0:27:09.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,like I think there's going to be a lot of demand for them.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:09.09,0:27:16.59,Sub,,0,0,0,,And And I think fundamentally, you know, with Nvidia being such a bottleneck, like we'll probably see, you know, more alternative accelerators.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:16.64,0:27:18.76,Sub,,0,0,0,,That being said, you know, there's bottlenecks further down the pipe.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:18.81,0:27:21.32,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, you know, there's like TSMC and ASML.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:21.37,0:27:24.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Maybe like a deeper bottleneck to all of this anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:24.63,0:27:29.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but, you know, long term, I think monopolies don't always last.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:29.80,0:27:33.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so, I I'm I think it'd be healthy for the market to have more alternative.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:33.36,0:27:35.49,Sub,,0,0,0,,As much as I love Nvidia, like to make that clear.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:35.54,0:27:38.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, I mean, they're obviously an amazing company and with an amazing product.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:38.63,0:27:42.58,Sub,,0,0,0,,Um I I do expect to see a little bit more divers- diversity in in the market.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:42.63,0:27:46.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,I also also thinks, you know, like Cerebras and Groq and these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:46.28,0:27:49.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, what are your thoughts on like some of those uh providers?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:49.72,0:27:50.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think they're pretty exciting.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.76,0:27:54.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, and and you see them doing really well on on certain workloads.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:54.16,0:27:59.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,And, you know, there there's some interesting, you know, people doing these like hybrid, you know, disaggregated inference where they run,
Dialogue: 0,0:27:59.68,0:28:04.63,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, Nvidia for the prefill and and Cerebras for the decode and and things like that. heard of that, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:04.68,0:28:05.84,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah, and, you know, Groq, too.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:05.89,0:28:10.14,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, cuz a lot of these things, you know, certain things are compute bound, certain things are memory bound.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:10.19,0:28:11.92,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, you can sort of mix and match.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:11.97,0:28:13.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh and I think that's quite exciting.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.88,0:28:17.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,It It starts to get very complex when you're deploying these things in practice.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:17.52,0:28:24.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh but but I I I do think there's a lot of There's a lot of, you know, opportunity in in in in these sort of, you know, more complex hardware setups.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:24.96,0:28:29.93,Sub,,0,0,0,,Are there any learnings that you get from uh some of these neo clouds, like I don't know,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:29.98,0:28:34.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,like Nebius or whatever, and like the way that they're doing things versus like what you're doing?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:34.48,0:28:40.35,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think one of the things that, you know, is very interesting with with neo clouds is like how can they expand so quickly?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:40.40,0:28:45.71,Sub,,0,0,0,,I I think actually the most crazy example is like Nscale, which went from like nowhere to like, you know, having like,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:45.76,0:28:51.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, whatever, hundreds of billions of dollars in in the pipeline despite barely having any capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.60,0:28:53.13,Sub,,0,0,0,,How can neo clouds grow so fast?
Dialogue: 0,0:28:53.18,0:28:56.03,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, there's like an you know, and and and basically the answer is like, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:56.08,0:28:59.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,and and this might be obvious, but like what they do is like they go out to like,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:59.85,0:29:09.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,you know, Anthropic or or or or OpenAI or some some big buyer or whatever and they basically say like, "Hey, do you want to buy like 5 years of chips?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:09.44,0:29:11.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,You know, sign this contract, we give you a good rate."
Dialogue: 0,0:29:11.28,0:29:14.97,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then they take that contract and then they go to, you know, Wall Street and say, "Look,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:15.02,0:29:21.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,we got this like, you know, big buyer, you know, they they committed to $10 billion worth of chips.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:21.28,0:29:22.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh we just need the money right now."
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.72,0:29:23.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then they go on to raise the money.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:23.96,0:29:29.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then they like, you know, go to like Supermicro and Dell or whatever and Nvidia and like get the hardware and then they install it.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:29.46,0:29:32.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And then, you know, now they have like, you know, deliver it to the customer, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:29:32.84,0:29:40.04,Sub,,0,0,0,,So so you have this like very nice sort of financial construct where you can basically sort of pre-sell things that you haven't even bought.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:40.09,0:29:43.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,And and that means, you know, you can scale up extremely fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:43.30,0:29:47.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,And so that's what we've seen with these neo clouds is is is they can scale very, very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:47.84,0:29:53.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think Modal, because we've always had a little bit more of a PLG focus and and and not the sort of, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:53.42,0:29:59.66,Sub,,0,0,0,,ability to lock in long-term contracts in the same way, it it's a little bit more challenging from a financial perspective to scale that fast.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:59.71,0:30:04.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh even though I think, you know, in the long run, like we'll get to the same point.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:04.12,0:30:10.00,Sub,,0,0,0,,But I think that's been kind of a fascinating thing to see with these neo clouds and especially like CoreWeave and and those big ones,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:10.05,0:30:11.18,Sub,,0,0,0,,um they've been very,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:11.23,0:30:18.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,very savvy with, you know, how they raise money and you know, how to, you know, think about GPU as collateral for loans and all these things.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:18.44,0:30:24.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,What's the relevance of like I I forget who it was, but like some like financial company was like,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:24.11,0:30:26.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,"Oh, we're going to make" Oh, I think it was Nvidia, actually.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:26.24,0:30:30.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,They were they were like, "We are going to turn GPUs into an asset class."
Dialogue: 0,0:30:30.86,0:30:35.16,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is that just cuz like they need to raise money and they're like trying to figure out where to get the money from?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.21,0:30:36.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like, what's the relevance of that?
Dialogue: 0,0:30:37.00,0:30:39.46,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean, there's a bunch of startups, I don't know if you're thinking about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:39.51,0:30:43.33,Sub,,0,0,0,,There's like Silicon Data and Computer Exchange and like Orin and and and a
Dialogue: 0,0:30:43.38,0:30:47.34,Sub,,0,0,0,,few other ones that are like basically like trying to get to like you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.39,0:30:52.67,Sub,,0,0,0,,creating price indices and indexes and and and trading derivatives and things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:52.72,0:30:53.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think it's interesting.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:53.92,0:30:59.11,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I I think with compute like it does there are a number of challenges with compute as an asset class.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:59.16,0:31:02.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like it it's definitely not as homogeneous as other asset classes.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:02.96,0:31:11.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,Uh you have different network and different locations and and and different disks and and CPUs and all kinds of stuff and reliability.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:11.24,0:31:15.06,Sub,,0,0,0,,I mean that being said like you can say the same thing about oil and like we kind of created like you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.11,0:31:18.23,Sub,,0,0,0,,relatively commoditized, you know, tradeable assets out of oil.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:18.28,0:31:19.45,Sub,,0,0,0,,It remains to be seen.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.50,0:31:20.78,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like I do think, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:20.83,0:31:26.54,Sub,,0,0,0,,at the scale where we are with the sort of AI like data center GPU deployments like we do need to
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.59,0:31:31.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,be a little bit smarter with like risk hedging and and and and how we share risks and and and you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:32.00,0:31:35.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,having more like sort of insurance and and things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:35.69,0:31:39.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, I I I I I I'm I'm very happy that people are thinking a lot about this.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:39.84,0:31:45.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,That being said like I'm I'm I'm not entirely sure if we're going to see, you know, GPUs becoming sort of, you know,
Dialogue: 0,0:31:46.00,0:31:53.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,whatever the sort of Henry Hub like, you know, Brent crude type like, you know, super commoditized like tradeable asset.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.04,0:31:54.48,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:54.53,0:31:58.91,Sub,,0,0,0,,I want to shift the conversation to Modal Sandboxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:58.96,0:31:59.47,Sub,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.52,0:32:03.19,Sub,,0,0,0,,I guess like before we do that, what are the different products that Modal has?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:03.24,0:32:07.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,It's I guess like the main product obviously is like the the GPUs.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.70,0:32:09.07,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then you have Modal Sandboxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:09.12,0:32:10.39,Sub,,0,0,0,,Is there anything else?
Dialogue: 0,0:32:10.44,0:32:16.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,I think of the like the two big products that we have is basically number one is Modal Functions and number two is Modal Sandboxes.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:16.92,0:32:20.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,So, so with Modal Functions we we launched that, you know, back in 2021.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:21.00,0:32:27.31,Sub,,0,0,0,,It was the idea of like serverless functions that are very very easy to deploy and very easy to scale and we manage all the capacity.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:27.36,0:32:33.27,Sub,,0,0,0,,That turned out to be really really good for inference and it turned out to be really good for managing GPUs and and running on things like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:33.32,0:32:38.05,Sub,,0,0,0,,But we actually never had like, you know, dedicated like inference product or like a GPU product per se.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.10,0:32:40.81,Sub,,0,0,0,,Like we we we never thought of Modal as like a Neo Cloud and and I
